1
00:03:08,520 --> 00:03:09,560
The doctor said…

2
00:03:09,640 --> 00:03:10,440
PREVIOUSLY

3
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:11,840
…you lost the baby.

4
00:03:12,800 --> 00:03:15,160
-Blood…
-I want to take care of you, Father.

5
00:03:15,800 --> 00:03:16,920
And take care of my daughter.

6
00:03:17,520 --> 00:03:19,480
Please give me one more chance.

7
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:21,040
-Enough, Dad.
-Step closer and I'll shoot.

8
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:28,680
Aren't you happy to see me?

9
00:03:30,080 --> 00:03:32,800
I even brought your favorite fruit.

10
00:03:43,600 --> 00:03:45,120
I'll peel some for you.

11
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:47,360
Nuch.

12
00:03:48,520 --> 00:03:49,520
I'm sorry.

13
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:52,840
I never meant to hurt you.

14
00:03:53,800 --> 00:03:55,240
You didn't mean to?

15
00:03:57,560 --> 00:03:59,800
You were pointing a gun at me.

16
00:04:00,960 --> 00:04:02,840
If Papang hadn't stopped you,

17
00:04:02,920 --> 00:04:04,760
I could've been shot.

18
00:04:09,120 --> 00:04:10,480
I was wrong.

19
00:04:11,640 --> 00:04:13,120
I take full responsibility.

20
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:17,279
I'm going to change.

21
00:04:17,360 --> 00:04:19,320
Once I leave the hospital,

22
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,880
I'll turn myself in
and face the consequences.

23
00:04:24,760 --> 00:04:28,280
I'm sorry. Give me a chance
to take care of you and our son.

24
00:04:29,960 --> 00:04:32,520
Someone like you
is going to accept responsibility?

25
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,120
You're selfish.

26
00:04:38,680 --> 00:04:40,800
All this nice talk,

27
00:04:40,880 --> 00:04:42,880
all these good deeds,

28
00:04:43,520 --> 00:04:45,640
you're just doing it for my forgiveness.

29
00:04:47,520 --> 00:04:49,120
Someone like you

30
00:04:50,160 --> 00:04:51,600
-deserves to die by my hand.
-Hey!

31
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:53,760
-I'll kill you.
-Stop, Nuch! Calm down.

32
00:04:55,160 --> 00:04:57,640
Nuch, I'm sorry.

33
00:04:57,720 --> 00:04:59,640
I want to take care of our son.

34
00:04:59,720 --> 00:05:01,680
Please give me a chance.

35
00:05:02,280 --> 00:05:03,840
It's too late.

36
00:05:05,320 --> 00:05:08,240
My son deserves to grow up
in a decent society.

37
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:11,320
He shouldn't know
his father is a corrupt man

38
00:05:11,400 --> 00:05:12,960
who cheats other people.

39
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:14,520
Nuch.

40
00:05:15,080 --> 00:05:18,240
Think carefully. If you kill me,

41
00:05:18,320 --> 00:05:19,680
you'll be punished.

42
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:23,640
Then what happens to our son?
Who will take care of him?

43
00:05:23,720 --> 00:05:26,280
Ramil and Hathaya.

44
00:05:27,080 --> 00:05:29,880
They can take care of my son.

45
00:05:31,760 --> 00:05:35,160
I'm willing to risk my life for this.

46
00:05:39,240 --> 00:05:41,920
My son deserves a good life.

47
00:05:42,840 --> 00:05:44,480
He doesn't need a bad father like you.

48
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:49,160
Someone like you deserves to die.

49
00:05:49,240 --> 00:05:50,440
Mommy!

50
00:05:54,080 --> 00:05:55,800
Mommy, don't hurt Daddy.

51
00:05:57,200 --> 00:05:59,040
This terrible man

52
00:06:00,120 --> 00:06:01,720
is not your father.

53
00:06:01,800 --> 00:06:04,560
Daddy Raiwin is my father.

54
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:16,360
A giant monster got inside Daddy
and made him hurt Mommy.

55
00:06:16,440 --> 00:06:18,600
Daddy Ramil already killed the monster.

56
00:06:18,680 --> 00:06:22,400
Daddy Raiwin is hurt now.
I want to help him get better.

57
00:06:23,360 --> 00:06:24,920
Aunt Hathaya.

58
00:06:25,720 --> 00:06:27,960
The bad giant got inside Mommy too.

59
00:06:28,040 --> 00:06:30,200
Please kill the giant.

60
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,720
I think

61
00:06:36,240 --> 00:06:38,840
the two of you
have hurt each other enough.

62
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:42,160
Please stop.

63
00:06:46,440 --> 00:06:48,000
Daddy Raiwin.

64
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,760
You won't hurt anymore.

65
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,280
I have magic medicine.

66
00:06:53,360 --> 00:06:55,760
I'm going to make you better.

67
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:02,440
Papang, my son.

68
00:07:05,960 --> 00:07:07,320
I'm sorry.

69
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,360
I love you.

70
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:35,160
I'm sorry. I really lost control.

71
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,920
It's not too late.

72
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,160
Your son's love can help heal you.

73
00:07:43,280 --> 00:07:46,600
I think I need to
move forward with my life.

74
00:07:46,680 --> 00:07:49,600
I'm going to find work
in another province.

75
00:07:49,680 --> 00:07:53,040
Once I've saved enough money,
I'll come back and live with my son.

76
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:58,000
Please take care of Papang for me.

77
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:02,840
You don't have to worry.
You know Hathaya and I

78
00:08:02,920 --> 00:08:04,320
love Papang like our own son.

79
00:08:05,400 --> 00:08:08,360
Everyone has been through terrible things.

80
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,360
I'm rooting for you.

81
00:08:10,440 --> 00:08:12,240
I believe that one day,

82
00:08:12,320 --> 00:08:14,880
you'll be strong enough
to stand tall again

83
00:08:14,960 --> 00:08:16,720
to protect your son

84
00:08:16,800 --> 00:08:19,480
and to give love to people who need it.

85
00:08:20,560 --> 00:08:22,120
Thank you.

86
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:27,960
Can I hug you goodbye?

87
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:44,480
Be careful. She's dangerous.

88
00:09:01,160 --> 00:09:02,800
What did Nuchwara say to you?

89
00:09:04,120 --> 00:09:04,960
You want to know?

90
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,920
I'm not telling you.

91
00:09:23,560 --> 00:09:25,080
Saksit called.

92
00:09:25,160 --> 00:09:27,720
He said Raiwin tricked him
into meeting Ramil

93
00:09:27,800 --> 00:09:31,120
because he's planning to turn himself in.
Saksit shot Raiwin and then ran.

94
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:33,200
How heartless can someone be?

95
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:35,480
A father willing to kill his own son.

96
00:09:36,080 --> 00:09:37,840
If he betrays me,

97
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:39,800
I won't let him get away with it.

98
00:09:40,600 --> 00:09:43,160
And what if it were me?
What would you do then?

99
00:09:51,400 --> 00:09:53,520
Just don't betray me, Mom.

100
00:09:55,480 --> 00:09:56,400
So…

101
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:59,520
what do we do now?

102
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:03,200
I'll use the same plan.

103
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:05,880
I'll trick Saksit into helping us escape.

104
00:10:06,480 --> 00:10:08,240
I don't trust him.

105
00:10:08,320 --> 00:10:11,880
If he finds out
we don't have any money, he'll kill us.

106
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,480
I already told you.

107
00:10:14,160 --> 00:10:16,440
I have nothing left to lose.

108
00:10:16,520 --> 00:10:19,520
Saksit is the only person
who can get us out.

109
00:10:29,560 --> 00:10:30,840
Chamoi.

110
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,480
Chamoi.

111
00:10:35,440 --> 00:10:36,480
It's me.

112
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:39,560
Chamoi.

113
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:41,400
Chamoi.

114
00:10:43,400 --> 00:10:44,360
Oh my God!

115
00:10:45,040 --> 00:10:48,800
Mom, I ordered food.

116
00:10:50,440 --> 00:10:51,640
Mom?

117
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,560
Where did you go?

118
00:11:00,600 --> 00:11:01,800
Why did you call me?

119
00:11:02,880 --> 00:11:05,440
Chamoi, open the gate.

120
00:11:05,520 --> 00:11:06,800
I need to see Father.

121
00:11:06,880 --> 00:11:09,920
No. You tried to hurt him.

122
00:11:10,760 --> 00:11:12,840
I need to talk to him.

123
00:11:13,680 --> 00:11:15,440
I admit I was wrong.

124
00:11:15,520 --> 00:11:17,640
Please. Open the gate
and let me see Father.

125
00:11:17,720 --> 00:11:21,040
No. You've done too many terrible things.

126
00:11:21,760 --> 00:11:24,640
I'm never letting you
set foot in this house again.

127
00:11:24,720 --> 00:11:26,240
I'm calling the police.

128
00:11:26,320 --> 00:11:29,200
Chamoi, please.

129
00:11:29,280 --> 00:11:31,640
Don't call them yet.
Let me see Father first.

130
00:11:32,360 --> 00:11:35,600
Open the gate.
Please let me in. I'm scared.

131
00:11:36,800 --> 00:11:39,760
Now you're scared? When you
were doing all those terrible things,

132
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:41,320
why weren't you scared then?

133
00:11:41,400 --> 00:11:43,880
Then what do I have to do

134
00:11:44,400 --> 00:11:45,960
before you'll let me in?

135
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:48,600
Get down on your knees.

136
00:11:48,680 --> 00:11:50,640
Get down on your knees and beg me.

137
00:11:50,720 --> 00:11:53,080
Then I'll open the gate.

138
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:16,520
Chamoi, I beg you.

139
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:19,360
Now please let me in
so I can talk to Father.

140
00:12:20,040 --> 00:12:23,320
All right. I'll let you in.

141
00:12:29,080 --> 00:12:31,440
Pong! You're still alive? Let go of me!

142
00:12:31,520 --> 00:12:32,480
-Hey!
-Help!

143
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:33,560
My god!

144
00:12:33,640 --> 00:12:34,840
Someone help!

145
00:12:34,920 --> 00:12:36,400
Chamoi.

146
00:12:36,480 --> 00:12:38,120
-What happened?
-Madam.

147
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:40,800
Pong kidnapped Madam Liu.

148
00:12:40,880 --> 00:12:42,040
Pong?

149
00:12:42,120 --> 00:12:43,800
Chamoi, call the police.

150
00:12:43,880 --> 00:12:45,000
Quickly.

151
00:12:46,040 --> 00:12:47,880
Where are you going?

152
00:12:47,960 --> 00:12:49,440
To get the car and follow them.

153
00:12:49,520 --> 00:12:50,760
-Hurry.
-Okay.

154
00:12:51,640 --> 00:12:54,240
-Come here, you bitch.
-Pong.

155
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:55,480
-Let go.
-Go.

156
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:00,720
How did you survive?

157
00:13:00,800 --> 00:13:02,840
I survived to teach you something.

158
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:05,360
When you try to kill someone,

159
00:13:05,440 --> 00:13:07,200
you'd better make sure they're dead.

160
00:13:07,720 --> 00:13:10,720
-Otherwise, they'll come back to kill you.
-Don't.

161
00:13:10,800 --> 00:13:13,400
Just like I'm about to do now.

162
00:13:13,480 --> 00:13:14,440
No.

163
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:16,800
Come here.

164
00:13:20,240 --> 00:13:21,320
Come here.

165
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,240
Where are you going?

166
00:13:25,320 --> 00:13:26,200
Damn it.

167
00:13:27,720 --> 00:13:28,920
That hurt.

168
00:13:32,320 --> 00:13:33,520
I never thought

169
00:13:33,600 --> 00:13:35,440
you could be such a poisonous snake.

170
00:13:36,040 --> 00:13:39,280
I was stupid to underestimate you.
But you know what?

171
00:13:40,440 --> 00:13:41,360
Now…

172
00:13:41,440 --> 00:13:42,680
I'm smarter.

173
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,000
Don't!

174
00:13:50,560 --> 00:13:52,720
Please let me go.

175
00:13:52,800 --> 00:13:55,960
Whatever you want, I'll get it for you.

176
00:13:56,040 --> 00:13:58,840
-What?
-It hurts.

177
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,360
Someone like you?

178
00:14:00,440 --> 00:14:01,880
What do you have left?

179
00:14:01,960 --> 00:14:03,520
Nothing.

180
00:14:03,600 --> 00:14:05,240
What are you going to bargain with?

181
00:14:05,320 --> 00:14:08,440
I'll go back to Father.
I'll ask him to help me.

182
00:14:08,520 --> 00:14:10,440
After everything you've done?

183
00:14:10,520 --> 00:14:12,680
You think he'd help you? You idiot!

184
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,440
Today…

185
00:14:17,880 --> 00:14:19,080
I'm sending you straight to hell.

186
00:14:19,160 --> 00:14:20,600
Don't!

187
00:14:21,320 --> 00:14:23,080
Huh? Police?

188
00:14:24,040 --> 00:14:25,480
Hey!

189
00:14:25,560 --> 00:14:27,040
Run!

190
00:14:27,120 --> 00:14:28,680
There's no time. Quickly.

191
00:14:33,880 --> 00:14:36,800
Liu, Liu, come here.

192
00:14:36,880 --> 00:14:38,440
Come on. Get up.

193
00:14:38,520 --> 00:14:40,920
-Chamoi, help me. Get up.
-Hathai?

194
00:14:41,000 --> 00:14:42,080
-Hurry.
-Come on.

195
00:14:42,160 --> 00:14:43,520
Sit over there.

196
00:14:44,280 --> 00:14:45,680
Careful.

197
00:14:46,560 --> 00:14:48,880
Chamoi, call an ambulance.

198
00:14:50,240 --> 00:14:51,960
Why did you help me?

199
00:14:52,640 --> 00:14:54,360
I may not be a good person,

200
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:56,840
but I'm not evil enough

201
00:14:56,920 --> 00:14:58,920
to kick someone when they're about to die.

202
00:15:02,240 --> 00:15:03,880
Even though

203
00:15:03,960 --> 00:15:06,240
I really did want you dead

204
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:08,400
after everything you did to me.

205
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:19,520
Someone like you deserves
to pay for everything you've done.

206
00:15:19,600 --> 00:15:21,040
And the reason I came here

207
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:24,080
was to have the police
drag Pong off to prison.

208
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:28,400
I'm sorry.

209
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,960
I was wrong.

210
00:15:31,040 --> 00:15:34,360
If you want to kill me,
I wouldn't blame you.

211
00:15:34,960 --> 00:15:36,560
The truth is

212
00:15:36,640 --> 00:15:39,040
I could kill you right here.

213
00:15:39,960 --> 00:15:43,720
Then I could tell the police Pong did it.

214
00:15:45,320 --> 00:15:46,720
And I'm sure

215
00:15:46,800 --> 00:15:49,720
Chamoi would back me up.

216
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,200
But I won't.

217
00:15:58,920 --> 00:16:00,720
Because I made a promise to my daughter

218
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:04,320
and to my mother's spirit.

219
00:16:07,560 --> 00:16:09,560
I'm going to become a better person.

220
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:15,760
I'm not creating any more
bad karma with anyone.

221
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:21,760
And I'm giving you a chance

222
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,280
the same way Hathaya

223
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:28,600
and everyone else gave me one.

224
00:16:36,880 --> 00:16:38,240
Hathai.

225
00:16:41,160 --> 00:16:42,080
I…

226
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:44,240
Thank you.

227
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:47,240
Thank you so much.

228
00:16:49,560 --> 00:16:51,240
I'm sorry.

229
00:17:07,839 --> 00:17:10,160
Father, I need to speak to you.

230
00:17:11,760 --> 00:17:14,359
Ramil, call the police
and have her arrested.

231
00:17:15,000 --> 00:17:15,839
Yes, sir.

232
00:17:16,359 --> 00:17:18,359
Hathaya, take me back to rest.

233
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,680
Father.

234
00:17:28,079 --> 00:17:29,240
Father.

235
00:17:30,080 --> 00:17:31,800
I was wrong.

236
00:17:32,400 --> 00:17:34,880
If you call the police
and have me arrested,

237
00:17:34,960 --> 00:17:36,360
I'll accept it.

238
00:17:36,440 --> 00:17:37,800
But please

239
00:17:38,800 --> 00:17:40,800
help your granddaughter.

240
00:17:41,600 --> 00:17:43,800
You want me to help
an ungrateful granddaughter?

241
00:17:43,880 --> 00:17:46,160
A murderer who tried to kill me?

242
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:50,960
Chayanee did what she did
because Chayanee lost control.

243
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:52,560
She felt like she had no choice.

244
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:56,120
If you claim Chayanee lost control,

245
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:58,720
then where is she?
Why didn't she come with you?

246
00:17:59,400 --> 00:18:01,920
She's hiding.

247
00:18:02,760 --> 00:18:05,000
I came to beg you.

248
00:18:07,680 --> 00:18:11,280
You're the only person who can help us.

249
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:16,240
Father, Chayanee

250
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:18,720
is your own blood.

251
00:18:19,400 --> 00:18:21,280
Please forgive her.

252
00:18:22,520 --> 00:18:24,520
Chayanee is my own blood.

253
00:18:25,040 --> 00:18:27,600
And yet she tried to kill me twice.

254
00:18:28,720 --> 00:18:31,480
Meanwhile, you called
everyone else parasites.

255
00:18:32,080 --> 00:18:34,320
But those people loved me and helped me.

256
00:18:36,440 --> 00:18:37,800
Father.

257
00:18:40,480 --> 00:18:42,560
You can blame me.

258
00:18:42,640 --> 00:18:44,320
Blame Chayanee.

259
00:18:44,960 --> 00:18:46,680
I'll accept that.

260
00:18:48,080 --> 00:18:50,760
But please help her first

261
00:18:50,840 --> 00:18:53,360
before she does something even worse.

262
00:18:53,440 --> 00:18:55,040
Please, Father.

263
00:18:56,360 --> 00:18:57,360
Father…

264
00:18:58,840 --> 00:19:02,400
Liu, where is Chayanee?

265
00:19:06,440 --> 00:19:07,680
She is…

266
00:19:08,280 --> 00:19:10,640
planning to have Saksit help her escape

267
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:13,760
even though she has no money to pay him.

268
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:18,600
I'm afraid Saksit will kill her.

269
00:19:19,720 --> 00:19:20,720
Grandpa.

270
00:19:22,560 --> 00:19:25,440
Please let us go help Chayanee.

271
00:19:26,280 --> 00:19:28,560
I'll talk to her
and convince her to turn herself in.

272
00:19:31,680 --> 00:19:34,960
Go and bring Chayanee to me.

273
00:19:36,120 --> 00:19:38,080
If she truly regrets what she's done,

274
00:19:38,840 --> 00:19:40,200
I'll help make things easier.

275
00:19:42,760 --> 00:19:43,760
Father…

276
00:19:47,680 --> 00:19:48,800
Father.

277
00:19:59,640 --> 00:20:00,960
Father.

278
00:20:02,520 --> 00:20:05,360
Thank you so much

279
00:20:06,960 --> 00:20:09,000
for showing mercy to your granddaughter.

280
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:17,280
Liu, can you take us to Chayanee?

281
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:25,320
-Chayanee?
-Chayanee?

282
00:20:28,240 --> 00:20:31,680
She's not here. Maybe she went out
to buy something.

283
00:20:32,920 --> 00:20:33,960
Let's wait downstairs.

284
00:20:40,680 --> 00:20:41,520
Liu.

285
00:20:41,600 --> 00:20:43,240
Could you call her again?

286
00:20:43,320 --> 00:20:45,960
But don't tell her you're with us.
Or she won't come back.

287
00:20:46,040 --> 00:20:48,040
Okay. I'll call her.

288
00:20:54,040 --> 00:20:54,920
She picked up.

289
00:20:56,680 --> 00:20:58,600
Sweetheart, where are you?

290
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:01,240
I went out to buy something.
Where were you?

291
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:05,320
I came out to get you some food.
Where are you?

292
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,920
Come back to the room.

293
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:10,120
Who are you with?

294
00:21:14,120 --> 00:21:15,440
I'm alone.

295
00:21:16,520 --> 00:21:19,840
Liar. You brought them here to arrest me.

296
00:21:23,560 --> 00:21:26,600
Chayanee, listen to me.

297
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:30,120
I'm not going to prison
and letting those people spit in my face.

298
00:21:31,400 --> 00:21:33,120
Chayanee, listen.

299
00:21:33,200 --> 00:21:36,520
I talked to Grandpa. He said he would--

300
00:21:38,080 --> 00:21:38,920
Liu, move!

301
00:21:41,360 --> 00:21:42,720
Chayanee, come back!

302
00:21:42,800 --> 00:21:44,800
-Grandpa is going to help you.
-Chayanee.

303
00:21:45,360 --> 00:21:47,320
Chayanee. Hello?

304
00:21:47,400 --> 00:21:48,920
Chayanee, come back.

305
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:50,640
-Grandpa is going to help you.
-Chayanee

306
00:21:50,720 --> 00:21:51,880
No…

307
00:21:52,400 --> 00:21:54,320
She turned off her phone.

308
00:22:06,080 --> 00:22:08,800
What is this? You want me
to help you escape?

309
00:22:12,040 --> 00:22:12,960
Where's the money?

310
00:22:14,200 --> 00:22:17,280
Before you ask me about money,
how are you going to escape?

311
00:22:17,360 --> 00:22:18,640
You can't even save yourself.

312
00:22:18,720 --> 00:22:20,560
Me? Do you really think that?

313
00:22:20,640 --> 00:22:22,560
I have plenty of connections.

314
00:22:24,360 --> 00:22:26,000
Pong? You're still alive?

315
00:22:27,840 --> 00:22:31,720
Someone like me?
Even the Grim Reaper doesn't dare take me.

316
00:22:32,720 --> 00:22:35,400
Your mother was very lucky. She got away.

317
00:22:35,480 --> 00:22:36,920
What did you do to my mother?

318
00:22:37,000 --> 00:22:39,400
I was going to kill her.

319
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:42,760
But the police showed up, so she got away.

320
00:22:44,440 --> 00:22:47,120
That's fine. Because today
I'm killing you instead.

321
00:22:48,120 --> 00:22:49,160
Come closer if you dare.

322
00:22:51,120 --> 00:22:54,040
Enough. Put the guns down.

323
00:22:54,120 --> 00:22:57,000
If you don't want to die,
stop fighting each other.

324
00:22:57,600 --> 00:22:59,680
Pong…

325
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:02,640
has people near the border.

326
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:04,840
He's going to get us out.

327
00:23:04,920 --> 00:23:06,800
Someone like her?

328
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:11,520
This spoiled little brat has nothing left.
She can't afford to pay us.

329
00:23:15,640 --> 00:23:17,720
You don't have the money? You lied to me?

330
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,600
I have a way to get it.

331
00:23:19,680 --> 00:23:20,640
What?

332
00:23:20,720 --> 00:23:22,880
Kidnap Grandpa and demand ransom.

333
00:23:22,960 --> 00:23:25,480
Hathaya will do anything
to keep her Grandpa alive.

334
00:23:25,560 --> 00:23:28,840
Think about it. You'll get the money

335
00:23:28,920 --> 00:23:31,200
and you'll end the lives
of those parasites too.

336
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,280
Ramil.

337
00:23:39,560 --> 00:23:40,520
Fine.

338
00:23:41,720 --> 00:23:44,920
Pong, get your men ready.

339
00:23:46,480 --> 00:23:48,120
Before we leave,

340
00:23:51,200 --> 00:23:53,720
I want to settle the score

341
00:23:53,800 --> 00:23:55,800
with all of them properly.

342
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:01,000
MODEL HOME

343
00:24:01,080 --> 00:24:04,080
-This way, Grandpa.
-Sir.

344
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:07,520
On behalf of everyone here,

345
00:24:08,320 --> 00:24:11,200
thank you for trusting us
to build your dream community.

346
00:24:11,280 --> 00:24:12,280
Thank you very much.

347
00:24:13,160 --> 00:24:14,920
Thank you.

348
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:18,200
Welcome home, sir.

349
00:24:20,760 --> 00:24:22,720
Thank you. Thank you, everyone.

350
00:24:23,880 --> 00:24:26,520
Thank you for giving us this opportunity.

351
00:24:27,120 --> 00:24:30,160
Without you,
we'd still be wandering around.

352
00:24:39,280 --> 00:24:40,440
Sir.

353
00:24:47,280 --> 00:24:50,360
I'm the one who should thank all of you.

354
00:24:50,440 --> 00:24:52,240
Hooray!

355
00:24:52,320 --> 00:24:53,520
Thank you.

356
00:24:53,600 --> 00:24:55,120
Thank you.

357
00:24:56,960 --> 00:24:57,960
This way, sir.

358
00:24:58,040 --> 00:24:59,960
I'll show you inside.

359
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:01,840
I'll take Grandpa.

360
00:25:01,920 --> 00:25:06,120
I ordered lots of food
and desserts for the workers.

361
00:25:07,080 --> 00:25:10,080
You should help take care of them.
I can look around myself.

362
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:12,320
-Go ahead.
-Okay.

363
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:16,200
MODEL HOME

364
00:25:20,240 --> 00:25:23,200
Hathaya, go take care of the workers.

365
00:25:23,720 --> 00:25:24,920
I'll look after Grandpa.

366
00:25:28,920 --> 00:25:30,000
Come on.

367
00:25:38,480 --> 00:25:39,360
Wait.

368
00:25:39,440 --> 00:25:40,600
Yes?

369
00:25:40,680 --> 00:25:43,440
Before you go, can I ask you something?

370
00:25:43,520 --> 00:25:44,680
What?

371
00:25:45,680 --> 00:25:48,120
What did Nuchwara say to you?

372
00:25:49,840 --> 00:25:51,040
You want to know?

373
00:25:53,240 --> 00:25:54,280
I'm not telling you.

374
00:25:56,880 --> 00:25:58,200
Come on. Your mom's calling.

375
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:00,040
Come on.

376
00:26:01,960 --> 00:26:03,720
Isn't the house beautiful, Father?

377
00:26:04,360 --> 00:26:05,200
Yes.

378
00:26:05,720 --> 00:26:08,760
It looks good. Very tasteful. Very neat.

379
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:14,400
Pong.

380
00:26:15,880 --> 00:26:17,720
Father, let's go.

381
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:25,520
What are you doing?

382
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:31,000
Grandpa still hasn't come outside to eat.

383
00:26:31,080 --> 00:26:32,880
He must really like the house you built.

384
00:26:39,280 --> 00:26:40,520
Chayanee.

385
00:26:40,600 --> 00:26:41,960
Where's Mr. Pichai?

386
00:26:42,680 --> 00:26:43,840
Where's Hathai?

387
00:26:43,920 --> 00:26:45,360
They're not dead yet.

388
00:26:45,440 --> 00:26:46,960
Chayanee.

389
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:48,880
Where did you take Grandpa and my mom?

390
00:26:48,960 --> 00:26:50,640
-Tell me.
-Stay back!

391
00:26:50,720 --> 00:26:51,560
Hathaya.

392
00:26:51,640 --> 00:26:54,240
As long as I'm still here,

393
00:26:54,920 --> 00:26:57,360
Grandpa and your mom aren't safe.

394
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:59,120
What do you want?

395
00:26:59,200 --> 00:27:00,920
One hundred million.

396
00:27:02,080 --> 00:27:04,360
And everything in the safe.
Bring it all to me.

397
00:27:04,440 --> 00:27:07,160
Chayanee, I don't have that much money.

398
00:27:07,760 --> 00:27:08,960
I know

399
00:27:09,040 --> 00:27:11,560
Grandpa left everything to you.

400
00:27:11,640 --> 00:27:14,040
If you don't want
their bodies delivered back to you,

401
00:27:15,400 --> 00:27:16,840
bring me what I asked for.

402
00:27:18,520 --> 00:27:20,720
I'll send you the location.

403
00:27:32,440 --> 00:27:33,480
Ramil.

404
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:36,520
I'm worried about Mom and Grandpa.

405
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:39,360
What do we do?

406
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:41,400
We…

407
00:27:42,840 --> 00:27:44,200
We give Chayanee the money.

408
00:28:00,680 --> 00:28:01,560
Thank you.

409
00:28:05,080 --> 00:28:06,880
Chayanee sent the location.

410
00:28:08,240 --> 00:28:09,120
This is…

411
00:28:09,200 --> 00:28:10,280
Let's hurry.

412
00:28:15,320 --> 00:28:18,360
Madam, where are you going?

413
00:28:19,120 --> 00:28:20,360
I'm not running away.

414
00:28:21,120 --> 00:28:24,080
I saw Hathaya and Ramil
come in and then rush back out.

415
00:28:24,680 --> 00:28:25,960
I peeked in.

416
00:28:26,040 --> 00:28:29,320
Miss Hathaya opened the safe.

417
00:28:29,400 --> 00:28:32,160
Something bad must have happened.

418
00:28:32,240 --> 00:28:34,640
Chamoi, let's go to the development.

419
00:28:37,200 --> 00:28:38,280
Okay.

420
00:28:38,880 --> 00:28:39,960
Everyone.

421
00:28:40,960 --> 00:28:44,440
I heard Mr. Pichai and Ms. Hathai

422
00:28:45,080 --> 00:28:46,440
were kidnapped for ransom.

423
00:28:46,520 --> 00:28:47,920
-What?
-What?

424
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,840
I knew something was wrong.

425
00:28:50,480 --> 00:28:51,640
We have to save Mr. Pichai.

426
00:28:51,720 --> 00:28:53,480
Whatever you guys decide, I'm in.

427
00:28:53,560 --> 00:28:54,400
-I'm in.
-Yes.

428
00:28:54,480 --> 00:28:55,320
-Okay?
-Yes.

429
00:28:55,400 --> 00:28:57,360
-Come on.
-Let's go.

430
00:28:57,440 --> 00:28:58,560
What's going on?

431
00:28:58,640 --> 00:28:59,480
Sorry.

432
00:29:01,360 --> 00:29:02,680
Let's eat.

433
00:29:02,760 --> 00:29:04,920
Nothing.

434
00:29:05,440 --> 00:29:06,960
-Keep eating.
-Hey!

435
00:29:07,480 --> 00:29:08,480
Don't lie.

436
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:11,720
I heard Mr. Pichai and Hathai

437
00:29:11,800 --> 00:29:14,000
were kidnapped for ransom. Who took them?

438
00:29:17,480 --> 00:29:18,520
I don't know.

439
00:29:18,600 --> 00:29:21,160
I just overheard Chayanee talking to Boss.

440
00:29:22,400 --> 00:29:24,880
There. Ramil's back.

441
00:29:27,560 --> 00:29:28,800
The workers' quarters.

442
00:29:35,280 --> 00:29:36,600
Saksit.

443
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:40,120
You refused to give me money when I asked.

444
00:29:41,480 --> 00:29:43,440
So I had to do things this way.

445
00:29:43,520 --> 00:29:46,960
I was right not to support
a corrupt politician like you.

446
00:29:47,040 --> 00:29:50,680
You might want to save some of that

447
00:29:51,280 --> 00:29:52,720
self-righteousness

448
00:29:52,800 --> 00:29:55,960
for your beloved granddaughter.

449
00:30:02,920 --> 00:30:03,920
Chayanee.

450
00:30:04,640 --> 00:30:06,320
How could you do this? Stop.

451
00:30:06,960 --> 00:30:08,480
You've caused enough trouble.

452
00:30:08,560 --> 00:30:10,720
This sounds like a family matter.

453
00:30:11,360 --> 00:30:14,560
Nothing to do with us. Let's go.

454
00:30:28,720 --> 00:30:32,000
Chayanee says to leave the bag out front

455
00:30:32,080 --> 00:30:34,080
and go inside to get Grandpa and Mom.

456
00:30:35,880 --> 00:30:37,360
Chayanee.

457
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:39,960
Stop this. You've caused enough trouble.

458
00:30:40,040 --> 00:30:42,080
It's too late, Grandpa.

459
00:30:42,680 --> 00:30:44,360
It's never too late.

460
00:30:45,160 --> 00:30:47,040
If you truly want to change,

461
00:30:47,560 --> 00:30:49,320
I'll help lighten the consequences.

462
00:30:50,040 --> 00:30:51,160
And then what?

463
00:30:52,480 --> 00:30:55,760
I'll still go to prison.
I can't live with that, Grandpa.

464
00:30:55,840 --> 00:30:57,320
I'd rather kill myself.

465
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:58,760
Chayanee.

466
00:31:00,480 --> 00:31:01,920
If I ever hurt you

467
00:31:03,600 --> 00:31:06,320
or disappointed you, punish me.

468
00:31:06,840 --> 00:31:07,800
Let everyone else go.

469
00:31:08,560 --> 00:31:09,600
No.

470
00:31:13,360 --> 00:31:15,040
Hathaya has to die

471
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:18,120
before I can be happy.

472
00:31:18,200 --> 00:31:21,240
No. Don't hurt my daughter.

473
00:31:32,560 --> 00:31:33,520
They tricked us.

474
00:31:37,200 --> 00:31:38,440
-Hey!
-Open the door.

475
00:31:40,200 --> 00:31:43,360
-Let us out!
-Pong, let us out! Saksit!

476
00:31:45,040 --> 00:31:46,480
We can leave now.

477
00:31:46,560 --> 00:31:47,920
What about them?

478
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:51,760
Those parasites
will be heading to hell soon enough.

479
00:31:54,120 --> 00:31:55,080
The roof too.

480
00:31:55,160 --> 00:31:56,240
Keep going.

481
00:31:56,320 --> 00:31:57,440
Pong! Saksit!

482
00:31:57,520 --> 00:32:00,400
Today I'm sending you
back where you belong.

483
00:32:00,480 --> 00:32:01,840
You bastard!

484
00:32:16,240 --> 00:32:17,280
Hey.

485
00:32:23,320 --> 00:32:24,840
I have to go now.

486
00:32:25,960 --> 00:32:27,840
I'll say goodbye to you here, Grandpa.

487
00:32:29,320 --> 00:32:30,880
No, Chayanee.

488
00:32:30,960 --> 00:32:33,680
Let me go. I need to save my daughter.

489
00:32:33,760 --> 00:32:35,000
Untie me right now.

490
00:32:35,760 --> 00:32:37,200
By now, your daughter

491
00:32:37,960 --> 00:32:39,280
has probably burned to death.

492
00:32:40,440 --> 00:32:44,000
And soon the fire will spread here too.

493
00:32:45,480 --> 00:32:48,000
Then you can take care
of your daughter in your next life.

494
00:32:48,080 --> 00:32:51,440
No. Let me go. Let me go right now!

495
00:32:52,040 --> 00:32:53,160
Chayanee.

496
00:32:54,080 --> 00:32:55,880
You can't escape the karma.

497
00:32:57,600 --> 00:32:58,760
No…

498
00:33:03,280 --> 00:33:05,160
Boss, aren't we waiting for Chayanee?

499
00:33:05,240 --> 00:33:08,960
Why would I? I nearly bled
myself dry getting this money.

500
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:10,800
I'm not sharing it with anyone.

501
00:33:10,880 --> 00:33:12,480
What are you saying?

502
00:33:17,840 --> 00:33:19,040
You're helping me.

503
00:33:20,440 --> 00:33:22,360
I'll give you Pong's entire share.

504
00:33:31,960 --> 00:33:33,360
Wait for me!

505
00:33:38,240 --> 00:33:40,680
-Ramil.
-Come here.

506
00:33:43,920 --> 00:33:45,600
Hathaya. Are you okay?

507
00:33:47,240 --> 00:33:50,360
Let me out! I need to save my daughter.

508
00:33:50,440 --> 00:33:53,600
Help! Someone help us!

509
00:33:58,440 --> 00:33:59,360
Someone help us!

510
00:33:59,440 --> 00:34:00,400
That's Hathai's voice.

511
00:34:00,480 --> 00:34:01,640
-Hurry.
-Help us!

512
00:34:01,720 --> 00:34:02,840
-Mr. Pichai's there!
-Hurry.

513
00:34:02,920 --> 00:34:03,920
-Come on.
-There!

514
00:34:04,000 --> 00:34:05,720
Go, go!

515
00:34:05,800 --> 00:34:06,800
Help!

516
00:34:06,880 --> 00:34:08,719
-Help me!
-There!

517
00:34:08,800 --> 00:34:09,800
-Father!
-Liu!

518
00:34:09,880 --> 00:34:12,480
Liu. Help me. Untie me.

519
00:34:12,560 --> 00:34:14,199
-Help me. I need to help Hathaya.
-Help me, quickly!

520
00:34:18,800 --> 00:34:20,239
Father.

521
00:34:20,320 --> 00:34:21,480
Father.

522
00:34:21,560 --> 00:34:23,080
I need to go.

523
00:34:23,159 --> 00:34:24,199
Father.

524
00:34:24,280 --> 00:34:26,600
Go. Quickly.

525
00:34:27,840 --> 00:34:28,920
Watch your head.

526
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:30,400
-Hathaya, are you okay?
-Boss.

527
00:34:30,480 --> 00:34:32,120
Check on Mom and Grandpa.

528
00:34:32,639 --> 00:34:34,320
Your grandpa and Hathai are safe.

529
00:34:36,719 --> 00:34:38,440
-Hathaya.
-Grandpa.

530
00:34:38,520 --> 00:34:39,880
Hathaya…

531
00:34:44,040 --> 00:34:45,239
Where's Chayanee?

532
00:34:46,280 --> 00:34:48,920
Chayanee, Pong, and Saksit kidnapped us.

533
00:34:49,000 --> 00:34:50,400
But they're gone now.

534
00:34:51,000 --> 00:34:52,080
I'm calling the police.

535
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:55,360
I already did.
They won't get away with this.

536
00:34:58,800 --> 00:35:00,760
My people at the border are ready, Boss.

537
00:35:01,360 --> 00:35:03,360
Once we get there,
we can cross immediately.

538
00:35:04,440 --> 00:35:05,320
Good.

539
00:35:09,360 --> 00:35:10,680
Chayanee.

540
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:31,440
-You were going to abandon me.
-Chayanee.

541
00:35:31,520 --> 00:35:32,920
I'll get you out.

542
00:35:34,000 --> 00:35:36,240
Here's the money. Take it.

543
00:35:37,080 --> 00:35:38,520
Chayanee.

544
00:35:38,600 --> 00:35:41,120
-Chayanee.
-I'm not stupid.

545
00:35:41,720 --> 00:35:42,760
Chayanee, wait!

546
00:35:43,280 --> 00:35:44,520
No!

547
00:36:00,480 --> 00:36:03,600
Chayanee. Enough, sweetheart.

548
00:36:03,680 --> 00:36:05,000
Stop.

549
00:36:05,680 --> 00:36:07,560
I'll find a way to help you.

550
00:36:09,720 --> 00:36:12,680
-No one can help me now.
-Chayanee.

551
00:36:14,840 --> 00:36:16,160
Turn yourself in.

552
00:36:16,800 --> 00:36:18,160
Chayanee.

553
00:36:18,840 --> 00:36:21,320
Everyone loves you
and is worried about you.

554
00:36:22,880 --> 00:36:26,080
Admit what you did. You still
have a chance to live your life.

555
00:36:26,760 --> 00:36:28,760
No matter how terrible things get,

556
00:36:28,840 --> 00:36:31,280
there is always a way out.

557
00:36:33,960 --> 00:36:35,440
There's always a way out.

558
00:36:36,760 --> 00:36:37,640
Yes.

559
00:36:38,480 --> 00:36:39,880
There is.

560
00:36:44,800 --> 00:36:46,200
And my way out is…

561
00:36:46,920 --> 00:36:49,400
Don't, Chayanee. Don't. Don't.

562
00:36:50,040 --> 00:36:51,560
Don't, Chayanee.

563
00:36:53,480 --> 00:36:55,280
No… Chayanee.

564
00:37:09,720 --> 00:37:12,640
-Don't.
-Chayanee.

565
00:37:15,640 --> 00:37:17,160
-My girl!
-Miss Chayanee!

566
00:37:22,240 --> 00:37:23,480
Chayanee.

567
00:37:32,800 --> 00:37:34,400
No!

568
00:37:36,880 --> 00:37:38,240
Chayanee.

569
00:37:39,520 --> 00:37:40,520
Chayanee.

570
00:37:42,400 --> 00:37:43,920
I'm sorry.

571
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:47,720
This is my fault.

572
00:37:54,560 --> 00:37:56,760
Chayanee…

573
00:38:00,760 --> 00:38:02,520
After that,

574
00:38:03,600 --> 00:38:05,600
Raiwin turned himself in.

575
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:09,000
Besides confessing to his own crimes,

576
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:10,680
he told the police

577
00:38:10,760 --> 00:38:13,840
about all the corruption cases
he'd been involved in

578
00:38:14,360 --> 00:38:16,520
and implicated other people too.

579
00:38:17,560 --> 00:38:18,920
It became

580
00:38:20,120 --> 00:38:22,120
major news for quite a while, Grandma.

581
00:38:24,720 --> 00:38:27,480
Even after Raiwin went to prison,

582
00:38:30,680 --> 00:38:32,600
there were still a lot of people

583
00:38:34,080 --> 00:38:37,280
who admired him for finally
having the courage to tell the truth.

584
00:38:41,040 --> 00:38:42,880
Sometimes I think about it, Grandma.

585
00:38:43,920 --> 00:38:45,920
If Saksit had listened

586
00:38:47,120 --> 00:38:48,920
to his son just a little more,

587
00:38:50,120 --> 00:38:51,880
or if Raiwin

588
00:38:52,960 --> 00:38:55,360
had stood by his own beliefs more firmly,

589
00:38:56,200 --> 00:38:58,240
someone like Raiwin

590
00:38:58,320 --> 00:39:01,480
might have become
a national-level politician.

591
00:39:04,480 --> 00:39:05,920
As for Ramil,

592
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:08,240
he moved out of here some time ago.

593
00:39:10,400 --> 00:39:12,680
He took Aunt Sanguansri with him.

594
00:39:14,640 --> 00:39:17,240
They moved into the house
Uncle Anon bought for them.

595
00:39:20,560 --> 00:39:21,880
Uncle Anon…

596
00:39:23,440 --> 00:39:24,840
tried…

597
00:39:25,720 --> 00:39:27,640
and failed so many times…

598
00:39:29,080 --> 00:39:31,440
because he thought what mattered
was buying a big house.

599
00:39:32,960 --> 00:39:34,200
But I think

600
00:39:35,280 --> 00:39:37,120
it doesn't matter where we live.

601
00:39:38,160 --> 00:39:40,440
If the people we love are together,

602
00:39:41,800 --> 00:39:42,640
that's what makes

603
00:39:43,640 --> 00:39:45,320
a real home.

604
00:39:47,360 --> 00:39:50,080
And that's what Ramil wanted all along.

605
00:39:51,880 --> 00:39:54,560
Grandpa is still sad sometimes, Grandma.

606
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:57,320
But my mom

607
00:39:58,000 --> 00:40:00,280
is always there taking care of him.

608
00:40:01,720 --> 00:40:03,360
And Papang is here too.

609
00:40:04,800 --> 00:40:06,800
Papang goes back and forth

610
00:40:07,600 --> 00:40:09,800
between this house and Ramil's house.

611
00:40:11,080 --> 00:40:12,920
Papang says he likes
staying with Great-Grandpa.

612
00:40:14,880 --> 00:40:17,520
And even though he never says it,

613
00:40:19,160 --> 00:40:20,760
I can tell

614
00:40:21,800 --> 00:40:25,360
he's getting more
and more attached to me too.

615
00:40:29,000 --> 00:40:30,840
It makes me think

616
00:40:32,400 --> 00:40:35,040
about how love and hate

617
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:38,320
can change.

618
00:40:40,400 --> 00:40:42,840
Just like Papang opened his heart to me.

619
00:40:44,200 --> 00:40:46,040
Just like Grandpa and Mom

620
00:40:46,920 --> 00:40:49,000
opened their hearts
and listened to each other.

621
00:40:50,640 --> 00:40:52,760
Grandma, you know,

622
00:40:52,840 --> 00:40:54,720
Grandpa and Mom are so close now.

623
00:40:55,480 --> 00:40:57,560
They go everywhere together.

624
00:41:00,000 --> 00:41:01,240
So…

625
00:41:04,320 --> 00:41:06,280
you don't need to worry about us anymore.

626
00:41:07,880 --> 00:41:10,880
I'll bring you lots more fun stories

627
00:41:12,320 --> 00:41:14,160
another time.

628
00:41:17,280 --> 00:41:19,440
But don't worry. It won't be anytime soon.

629
00:41:20,800 --> 00:41:22,320
You'll have to wait.

630
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:32,840
As for Aunt Liu…

631
00:41:37,600 --> 00:41:40,160
Chayanee, after you…

632
00:41:44,480 --> 00:41:45,960
left us…

633
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:52,560
Aunt Liu was arrested.

634
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:55,400
The evidence against her was overwhelming.

635
00:41:58,160 --> 00:42:00,360
But even without it,

636
00:42:04,120 --> 00:42:07,880
I don't think she had
the strength left to fight anymore.

637
00:42:10,320 --> 00:42:12,760
After everything that happened,

638
00:42:14,440 --> 00:42:16,560
everyone in the family agreed

639
00:42:19,240 --> 00:42:21,760
that she had already lost
more than enough.

640
00:42:24,440 --> 00:42:27,480
It was probably
more than anyone could bear.

641
00:42:32,760 --> 00:42:34,600
When she finishes serving her sentence,

642
00:42:35,920 --> 00:42:39,720
everyone here will still welcome her home.

643
00:42:42,480 --> 00:42:44,240
So don't worry, Chayanee.

644
00:42:56,360 --> 00:42:57,320
And…

645
00:43:00,200 --> 00:43:02,760
what I regret most…

646
00:43:07,520 --> 00:43:09,520
is that I never got the chance

647
00:43:10,320 --> 00:43:13,440
to make things right with you.

648
00:43:21,520 --> 00:43:25,360
I still remember when we were little.

649
00:43:27,680 --> 00:43:30,640
You and I were so close.

650
00:43:35,040 --> 00:43:37,320
But everything that happened,

651
00:43:38,480 --> 00:43:39,720
I know

652
00:43:40,320 --> 00:43:42,720
it didn't begin with the two of us.

653
00:43:44,560 --> 00:43:46,600
And I still don't understand

654
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:52,240
how we ended up fighting
until everything went so far.

655
00:44:05,520 --> 00:44:07,880
If I could change anything,

656
00:44:11,600 --> 00:44:14,840
I would try harder to talk to you.

657
00:44:16,800 --> 00:44:18,400
I'm sorry…

658
00:44:21,160 --> 00:44:23,320
I wasn't good enough.

659
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:29,280
I'm sorry.

660
00:44:33,240 --> 00:44:34,760
I played a part

661
00:44:35,880 --> 00:44:40,040
in making you choose what you did.

662
00:44:49,760 --> 00:44:51,400
I truly am sorry.

663
00:44:56,440 --> 00:44:58,800
And if there really is another life,

664
00:45:01,000 --> 00:45:03,640
I hope we meet again.

665
00:45:06,360 --> 00:45:08,880
You can be my little sister again.

666
00:45:12,440 --> 00:45:14,760
You don't have to worry anymore, Chayanee.

667
00:45:29,120 --> 00:45:30,440
Grandpa.

668
00:45:31,440 --> 00:45:34,120
I'm going to visit Aunt Liu.
Anything you want me to tell her?

669
00:45:34,200 --> 00:45:35,200
Hm.

670
00:45:36,040 --> 00:45:39,480
Tell her to take care of herself.
And not to dwell on everything too much.

671
00:45:40,680 --> 00:45:41,960
And tell her that

672
00:45:42,040 --> 00:45:44,080
when she finishes her sentence,

673
00:45:44,160 --> 00:45:46,280
we can all be together again.

674
00:45:48,640 --> 00:45:50,720
And visit Raiwin for me too.

675
00:45:51,360 --> 00:45:54,280
Okay. Actually,

676
00:45:54,360 --> 00:45:56,680
I just visited him a few days ago.

677
00:45:58,000 --> 00:46:00,240
He's doing well mentally

678
00:46:00,320 --> 00:46:02,520
and helping with work in prison.

679
00:46:02,600 --> 00:46:04,920
I believe he'll be released
before too long.

680
00:46:07,720 --> 00:46:09,480
Mr. Pichai, sir!

681
00:46:10,480 --> 00:46:11,800
You scared me.

682
00:46:11,880 --> 00:46:13,920
That voice could shatter glass.

683
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:15,840
Maybe I should send you
to construction work.

684
00:46:15,920 --> 00:46:17,600
No, sir.

685
00:46:18,720 --> 00:46:23,200
Sir, there's a very special guest
here to see you.

686
00:46:23,800 --> 00:46:25,920
Who? How special could they be?

687
00:46:30,240 --> 00:46:32,920
-Papang.
-Hello.

688
00:46:33,680 --> 00:46:36,800
How are you? How's the new house
your father bought for you?

689
00:46:36,880 --> 00:46:39,400
It's beautiful.
And I sleep very well there.

690
00:46:40,120 --> 00:46:41,960
Of course he does, Father.

691
00:46:42,040 --> 00:46:44,600
There's no Chamoi
screeching to hurt his ears.

692
00:46:44,680 --> 00:46:45,640
Right.

693
00:46:47,560 --> 00:46:50,400
Mr. Pichai, I came to
discuss something with you.

694
00:46:50,480 --> 00:46:52,720
I'd like to formally ask

695
00:46:52,800 --> 00:46:57,000
for your granddaughter's hand
in marriage for my son.

696
00:47:00,000 --> 00:47:01,760
What do you think?

697
00:47:01,840 --> 00:47:05,440
And how does your son
feel about my granddaughter?

698
00:47:07,320 --> 00:47:10,440
Do I really have to say it out loud, sir?

699
00:47:10,520 --> 00:47:11,800
I can get embarrassed too.

700
00:47:11,880 --> 00:47:14,120
I think you've already seen

701
00:47:14,200 --> 00:47:16,920
how much I love

702
00:47:17,000 --> 00:47:19,560
and care about your granddaughter.

703
00:47:19,640 --> 00:47:20,840
I know.

704
00:47:21,400 --> 00:47:25,240
Then I hope you have no objection to us
formally asking for her hand.

705
00:47:27,400 --> 00:47:28,360
Great-Grandpa.

706
00:47:28,440 --> 00:47:29,440
Yes?

707
00:47:30,040 --> 00:47:32,240
I have two daddies.

708
00:47:32,320 --> 00:47:33,160
Yes.

709
00:47:33,240 --> 00:47:35,640
Daddy Raiwin and Daddy Ramil.

710
00:47:36,280 --> 00:47:39,000
But I only have one mommy.

711
00:47:40,240 --> 00:47:43,520
I want Mommy Hathaya too.

712
00:47:44,800 --> 00:47:46,680
You're so important, right?

713
00:47:53,320 --> 00:47:56,720
Come here. Sit with me. Good boy.

714
00:47:57,320 --> 00:48:00,760
So you agree, right?

715
00:48:02,440 --> 00:48:03,280
No.

716
00:48:06,440 --> 00:48:07,720
Why not, sir?

717
00:48:07,800 --> 00:48:09,800
Why not, Grandpa?

718
00:48:10,320 --> 00:48:13,720
The last time someone came
to ask for your granddaughter's hand,

719
00:48:13,800 --> 00:48:16,240
you said it should be up to her.

720
00:48:16,320 --> 00:48:19,840
Why aren't you asking
how I feel this time?

721
00:48:21,960 --> 00:48:23,280
Hathaya.

722
00:48:23,880 --> 00:48:26,400
You're a woman. Try to hide
your excitement a little.

723
00:48:29,240 --> 00:48:32,520
I don't want you
marrying me off to someone else.

724
00:48:32,600 --> 00:48:34,040
Excuse me.

725
00:48:36,040 --> 00:48:36,920
Come here.

726
00:48:37,000 --> 00:48:39,840
If you don't give us your blessing,
I'll just run away with her.

727
00:48:44,080 --> 00:48:45,440
You'd really go that far?

728
00:48:47,720 --> 00:48:49,800
When I said no,

729
00:48:49,880 --> 00:48:53,200
I meant there's no need
to waste time with a formal proposal.

730
00:48:58,400 --> 00:49:01,280
Everyone already thinks you two

731
00:49:01,920 --> 00:49:03,480
are husband and wife anyway.

732
00:49:03,560 --> 00:49:05,640
So stop making such a fuss.

733
00:49:05,720 --> 00:49:07,640
No elaborate ceremony.

734
00:49:08,240 --> 00:49:10,280
Just take my granddaughter to your home

735
00:49:10,360 --> 00:49:12,960
and make her happy.

736
00:49:13,680 --> 00:49:15,440
Thank you so much, sir.

737
00:49:16,120 --> 00:49:17,480
Thank you, Grandpa.

738
00:49:18,200 --> 00:49:19,160
Ramil.

739
00:49:19,720 --> 00:49:22,080
Stop addressing me like that.

740
00:49:22,800 --> 00:49:23,760
Call me something else.

741
00:49:25,720 --> 00:49:27,800
Grandpa… Go ahead.

742
00:49:29,760 --> 00:49:31,720
Thank you, Grandpa.

743
00:49:32,560 --> 00:49:33,760
That's better.

744
00:49:36,840 --> 00:49:39,000
I just want to see my granddaughter happy

745
00:49:39,760 --> 00:49:41,760
and building a family based on love.

746
00:49:43,040 --> 00:49:44,000
I promise.

747
00:49:44,600 --> 00:49:47,880
I'll make Hathaya
the happiest woman in the world.

748
00:49:55,840 --> 00:49:57,480
Hug her. Kiss her.

749
00:49:57,560 --> 00:49:59,320
Come on, hug her.

750
00:49:59,400 --> 00:50:02,440
-Show some respect in front of Father.
-Oh, go ahead.

751
00:50:02,520 --> 00:50:03,560
I won't look.

752
00:50:06,320 --> 00:50:08,920
Then go ahead and kiss her.

753
00:50:09,000 --> 00:50:13,240
-Kiss her.
-Kiss her.

754
00:50:13,320 --> 00:50:15,200
-Kiss her.
-Kiss her.

755
00:50:15,280 --> 00:50:17,360
-Kiss her.
-Kiss her.

756
00:50:17,440 --> 00:50:18,760
All right.

757
00:50:19,600 --> 00:50:21,280
Wait!

758
00:50:21,360 --> 00:50:23,480
-What now?
-Wait.

759
00:50:23,560 --> 00:50:25,600
Why? Let me ask you something first.

760
00:50:26,560 --> 00:50:27,920
What did Nuchwara say to you?

761
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:30,360
Nuchwara warned me

762
00:50:30,440 --> 00:50:31,880
to be careful.

763
00:50:32,880 --> 00:50:34,120
You're dangerous.

764
00:50:37,120 --> 00:50:38,240
You still love me anyway?

765
00:50:38,840 --> 00:50:39,960
Of course I do.

766
00:51:15,120 --> 00:51:21,760
THE END

767
00:52:21,800 --> 00:52:22,640
Subtitle translation by: Thanit Puncharoen
